'''Point Tarron''' was a supposed location. During a [[Galactic Republic]] [[Battle of Lola Sayu|infiltration]] of the [[Citadel]] [[prison]] on [[Lola Sayu]] during the [[Clone Wars]], a group led by [[Jedi General]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] and including [[R2-D2's battle droid squadron|reprogrammed]] [[battle droid]]s attempted to reach their [[Shuttle 81572|shuttle]] on the prison's landing pad, after the [[astromech droid]] [[R2-D2]] and the battle [[droid]]s had freed them from being captured. [[OOM-10]], the reprogrammed droid in the lead, claimed to the droids guarding the [[shuttle]] that they were transferring their "[[prisoner]]s" to a supposed [[Confederacy of Independent Systems|Separatist]] outpost at Point Tarron. The ruse nearly worked, but the guard droids were alerted to the escape attempt by [[tactical droid]] [[K2-B4]], leading to a firefight at the landing platform and the eventual destruction of the shuttle.<ref name="Counterattack" />

==Behind the scenes==
The episode trivia guide for "[[Counterattack]]" words it that Point Tarron does not exist at all, saying that the fake outpost was Point Tarron.<ref name="Counterattack Episode Guide">{{SW|url=series/clone-wars/counterattack-episode-guide|text="Counterattack" Episode Guide &#124; The Clone Wars}}</ref>

